{"content":[{"c":["SUCCOTH-BENOTH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Deity and shrine worshiped by Babylonians settled in Samaria by Assyria after the fall of Israel in 722 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.17.30","r":"2Kgs.17.30","rawR":"2Kgs.17.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.17.30","value":"2Kgs.17.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 17:30"},"). Various opinions exist as to the specific understanding of Succoth-benoth. Some suggest that it refers to a place of prostitution honoring a Babylonian deity or to a small structure housing female idols. Others suggest it refers to Sarpanitu, the consort of Marduk (a Babylonian deity), or to Marduk himself."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"SuccothBenoth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 17:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.17.30","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.17.30","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.17.30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5d313b9b8151db0edf33d12e75725354866249d0db5d47deb9ebedf7d45e7e92","sourceItemName":"SuccothBenoth","sourceItemOrder":567,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"SuccothBenoth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Succoth-Benoth","title":"Succoth-Benoth","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}